# Secrets — the Groq key and DB URL live here
# Secrets. The bare `.env` rule this replaces matched ONLY the exact name, so
# .env.local / .env.production / .env.staging were all one `git add -A` away
# from being published. Ignore the whole family, then re-admit the two that are
# deliberately public: .env.example is a template, .env.test is localhost and a
# fake secret and exists so anyone can run the suite.
.env*
!.env.example
!.env.test

# Prisma generated client
server/generated/
expo-env.d.ts
# @end expo-cli

# Rendered portraits and the Python bytecode from the Blender pipeline.
# The renders are build output — reproducible from tools/portraits with a
# fixed seed — and a full library is hundreds of megabytes.
mobile/assets/portraits/
tools/**/__pycache__/

# Redis writes its snapshot into whatever directory it was started from, which
# is the server directory if you ran `redis-server` there. It is a database
# file, not source.
dump.rdb

# The suspect models are NOT ignored, deliberately.
#
# Metro resolves `require('@/assets/suspect/*.glb')` at bundle time, so a
# missing file is a build error rather than a missing texture — the app does
# not start without them. Reproducing them needs Blender, MPFB2 and a 268MB
# MakeHuman asset pack, which is not a reasonable thing to ask of a fresh
# checkout. They are build output that has to be in the tree; git LFS would be
# the better home if this grows.
